{#
    One borrowed sentence, and the element draws all of it.

    **Every option is a property**, and the sentence stands between the tags.
    That is the one thing about a quotation an attribute cannot hold, because
    out of a document it carries links and emphasis. Nothing here draws the
    attribution. Who said it, what they are to the subject and when are one
    row in one order, and that order is what the component is.
#}
{#- Where a reader can read a borrowed sentence in full is usually not in
    this manual. So the target stays as it is where it points off the site.
    It resolves where it points into it — the guard `card` puts on its
    picture. -#}
{%- set given = node.option('href') -%}
{%- set href = given ? (given is external_target ? given : renderLink(given)) : '' -%}
<sds-quote
    by="{{ node.option('by') }}"
    {%- if node.option('as') %} as="{{ node.option('as') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('meta') %} meta="{{ node.option('meta') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('initials') %} initials="{{ node.option('initials') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if href %} href="{{ href }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('class') %} class="{{ node.option('class') }}"{% endif %}
>
    {%- for child in node.children -%}
        {{ renderNode(child) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
</sds-quote>
